coverage:
Read in full: intro, setup (Sec 2), Sec 3 (stress-bending), Sec 7a (flux algebra), Sec 7 (preparation, lapse, profiles, equations, mass-loss estimate, final AH theorem and Lorentz balancing), Sec 11 (static Heintze-Karcher deficit and global identification), the statement of Thm 4.1 and the completion in Sec 5 (comparison metric, flux loss, Bray-Lee application), and the start of Sec 8 (equality multipliers).

Checked by hand or sympy:
- conformal preparation: Hamiltonian/momentum transforms, Neumann expansion sign, 6(e^{4v}-1)-24v>=0;
- the saturating law: s^2=t/(1-t^{3/2}) gives b=4(1-x)/(2+x);
- conserved stress: W'=3t/2, W-sW'=2k, L eigenvalues, (trL)^2-|L|^2=6, P:K<=0 under the one-sign stress, flat DEC of K+L, J unchanged, the K -> -K reduction for the other sign;
- flux saturation (coarea, uniform superlevel volume, Jensen/power mean);
- bending-end mass: p0(e^{4v}b)=avg 8v3, F_g expansion, E=avg(8v3-C^3/2), and the B expansion against the L eigenvalues. Spherical check: the Misner-Sharp mass of (g_SAdS, L) is M-C^3/2 with t=C^2/r^2, which is consistent and sharp as D->infinity;
- AH graph identity: q1^2 coefficient 12d/(4+pv)^2, the T completion, the coercivity identity, (1-chi)(4+pv)=(p+4)v, d-chi=pdv/(4+pv);
- conformal four-flux formula and error orders;
- SAdS normalization M=(r_h+r_h^3)/2;
- static HK identities (Green and divergence boundary terms, E and K+E identities, J/I>=3/2) and the deficit limit 4pi r^3(chi-2)/(3(6r^2+chi));
- numeric sanity check that Kerr-AdS (M=m/Xi^2) satisfies the inequality.

Not re-derived:
- the flat spacetime Penrose Thm 4.1 (Secs 4-6: generalized-Jang coupled system, floor exclusion, degree, rank-one regularity). The whole result depends on it; sibling papers in the same family use the same machinery;
- the Sec 7 existence and floor lemmas;
- the Sec 8 multiplier and adjoint analysis, Sec 9 twist and null-set exclusion, Sec 10 compactification, Sec 12 embedding (only skimmed);
- whether the cited Borghini-Fogagnolo-Pinamonti Thm 1.1 hypotheses match exactly (taken from the paper's own claim).
